            <Placemark id="22">
                <name>2.00in hail 14 SE Kent (10/27 7:55 PM CDT) - Confirmed: spotter/public report</name>
                <description>Basis: Confirmed: spotter/public report
Public report of egg sized hail that fell on their ranch property. (MAF)
SPC filtered hail 261027 (2.00" 14 SE Kent 0055Z = 7:55 PM CDT 10/27) = IEM/NWS LSR HAIL 2.00 (qualifier M, Public, NWS Midland). DISCREPANCY: LSR codes it "measured" but the remark is an object comparison ("egg sized") - treated as spotter/public (rank 2). MRMS MESH 24h ending 10/28 11:30Z: 2.80" at the report (2.80" swath centered on the report; second 2.30" pixel ~6 mi NW). HailTrace public 10/27 page lists the same report (shown there as 10/26 7:55 PM CDT - date label off by one day) and Fort Davis TX among impacted cities.</description>
                <Point id="21">
                    <coordinates>-104.04,30.93,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
